# Character layer checklist

When adding a **new customizable layer** under `Girl` (sprite renderer + items + wizard step):

## Scene & rendering

1. Add a child GameObject under `Girl` in `Assets/Scenes/MainScene.unity` (same pattern as `Crown` / `Glasses`).
2. Wire the `SpriteRenderer` on `CharacterCustomizer` (new serialized field if needed).
3. Add the layer to `CharacterLayerLayout.layerAnchors`.
4. Set `sortingOrder` in `CharacterCustomizer.ApplySortingOrders()`.
5. Update `GameSceneBuilder.CreateGirlCharacter()` for future scene rebuilds.
6. Tell the user to run **Dress Up Game → Reload Main Scene** so the new hierarchy appears in the Editor.

## Data & save position

7. Create item ScriptableObjects (and generator tool if many variants).
8. Update `GameCatalog` and any wizard/edit UI grids.
9. Add **Dress Up Game → Save {Layer} Position To {Item}** in `SaveLayerPositionTool.cs` (mirror Hair/Crown/Glasses pattern).
10. Include the layer in **Reset Layer Positions** and any offset-reset helpers.

## Wizard (if applicable)

11. Add a `WizardStep`, grid show method, and handler in `OpeningWizardController`.
12. Include a **None** option when the category supports skipping.

## Menu items to add every time

| Purpose | Menu path |
|---------|-----------|
| Save layout from Scene view | `Dress Up Game/Save {Layer} Position To {Item}` |
| Refresh hierarchy after scene edits | `Dress Up Game/Reload Main Scene` |

Never rely on runtime-only `new GameObject()` for layers the user must position in the Editor — persist them in `MainScene.unity`.
